`unified_strdate` always builds `upload_date` with `strftime('%Y%m%d')`, either from a successful `datetime.strptime(..., expression)` inside the date-format loop or from the `email.utils.parsedate_tz` fallback converted through `datetime(*timetuple[:6])`. So every observed `upload_date` is an 8-character digit string in `YYYYMMDD` form. Reading the 18 literals in the test suite and applying the matching formats/fallback yields these dates: 20140812, 20170503, 20190704, 20200315, 20180105, 20210422, 20150830, 20161122, 20180131, 20220615, 20190201, 20101231, 20240527, 20260704, 20240228, 20130910, 20200403, 20171207. From those values, length is always 8, `isdigit()` is always `true`, the first character is always `"2"`, and the mean of their integer values rounds to 20185609.44.

## Answer
{"first_char_invariant":true,"first_char_value":"2","isdigit_invariant":true,"isdigit_value":true,"length_invariant":true,"length_value":8,"mean_int_value":20185609.44,"observation_count":18}
